      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="legal-updated">Last updated: <%= legal.PRIVACY_EFFECTIVE_PRETTY %></p>

      <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
      <p>Legacy Odyssey ("Legacy Odyssey," "we," "us," or "our") is operated by <strong>DOR Industries</strong>, based in Mesa, Arizona, USA. Legacy Odyssey lets parents and guardians build a private website about their child. For the purposes of the EU and UK General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR / UK GDPR), DOR Industries is the <strong>data controller</strong> for personal data processed through the Service.</p>
      <p>The content you share with us is deeply personal: photos and videos of your children, their milestones, and your family's memories. This Privacy Policy explains what we collect, why, the legal bases we rely on, who we share it with, how long we keep it, and the rights you have.</p>
      <p><strong>Contact for privacy matters:</strong> <a href="mailto:help@legacyodyssey.com">help@legacyodyssey.com</a>.</p>

      <h2>2. Information we collect</h2>
      <h3>2.1 Account information</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Email address</li>
        <li>Account login password. This is handled by our authentication provider (Supabase Auth) and stored only as a salted hash; we never see your plain-text login password.</li>
        <li>Name and display name (optional)</li>
      </ul>
      <h3>2.2 Website viewing passwords</h3>
      <p>Each Legacy Odyssey Website has a separate <strong>viewing password</strong> that you choose and share with family and friends. This is different from your account login password. Because you need to be able to look it up and share it again, the viewing password is <strong>stored in a retrievable form, not as a one-way hash</strong>. It is shown to you (the account holder) in your account dashboard and in the app, and it may be included in emails we send to you about your website (for example, the email telling you your website is live). It is protected by the same access controls and encryption at rest as the rest of your data. Please do not reuse a password from another account as your viewing password. When a visitor enters the viewing password, we store a hashed token in a cookie on their browser so they do not have to re-enter it on every page.</p>
      <h3>2.3 Website content you provide</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Photos and images, including custom galleries and keepsake photos</li>
        <li>Videos (Video Moments)</li>
        <li>Text content (stories, letters, recipes, milestones, captions)</li>
        <li>Child information (name, birth date, birth details)</li>
        <li>Family member information (names, relationships)</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Some of this content relates to <strong>children</strong>. You provide it as the parent or legal guardian; see Section 12.</p>
      <h3>2.4 Your Contacts</h3>
      <p>If you use Your Contacts to share your website, we store the names, email addresses, and phone numbers of the people you add, the groups you put them in, and whether they have unsubscribed from update emails. If you allow the app to read your phone's contacts, the list is read on your device and only the contacts you choose are sent to us. We use contact details only to deliver the updates and private links you ask us to send. We email contacts on your behalf; text messages are sent from your own phone, not by us.</p>
      <h3>2.5 Gift purchases</h3>
      <p>When you buy a gift, we collect your name and email, the recipient's name and (if we are emailing the gift) their email, your personal note, and your delivery choice. When a gift is redeemed, we collect the recipient's email and chosen domain to create their account.</p>
      <h3>2.6 Payment information</h3>
      <p>Payments are processed by Stripe, Inc. We do <strong>not</strong> store your full card number, bank details, or other sensitive payment credentials on our servers. We keep limited billing records (for example transaction IDs, amounts, and dates) for accounting and tax purposes.</p>
      <h3>2.7 Domain information</h3>
      <p>If you choose a custom domain, we collect the domain name and the registrant details required to register it. Registration is handled by our registrar partner (Spaceship), subject to their privacy policy and to ICANN requirements.</p>
      <h3>2.8 Technical and usage information</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>IP address, browser type and version, device type</li>
        <li>Pages visited and actions taken on our marketing website and in the Service</li>
        <li>Date and time of access</li>
        <li>Error reports from our servers, which can include technical details of the request that failed</li>
        <li>Information collected by cookies and similar technologies (see Section 5)</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>3. How we use your information and legal bases</h2>
      <p>Where GDPR / UK GDPR applies, we rely on the following legal bases (Article 6):</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>To provide the Service</strong> (host your website, store and stream your content, translate it for visitors who choose another language, manage your account): <em>performance of a contract</em>.</li>
        <li><strong>To process payments and manage subscriptions, gifts, and domains:</strong> <em>performance of a contract</em>.</li>
        <li><strong>To send service emails</strong> (welcome, password reset, billing, website-live, important notices) and the contact updates you ask us to send: <em>performance of a contract</em> / <em>legitimate interests</em>.</li>
        <li><strong>To send product news and tips:</strong> <em>legitimate interests</em> (you can unsubscribe at any time from the link in every such email).</li>
        <li><strong>To keep records and meet tax, accounting, and legal obligations:</strong> <em>legal obligation</em>.</li>
        <li><strong>For analytics, advertising, and marketing cookies and pixels:</strong> <em>your consent</em> where required (which you can withdraw at any time), and otherwise subject to your right to opt out (Section 10).</li>
        <li><strong>To secure the Service, fix errors, and prevent abuse:</strong> <em>legitimate interests</em>.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>4. How we protect your information</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Encryption in transit:</strong> all traffic is served over HTTPS/TLS.</li>
        <li><strong>Encryption at rest and secure storage:</strong> data is stored with Supabase, which provides encryption at rest and regular backups. Photos are also backed up to a separate Cloudflare R2 storage bucket that we control.</li>
        <li><strong>Access controls:</strong> only authorized personnel can access your data, and only when needed to provide support or operate the Service.</li>
        <li><strong>Private websites:</strong> Legacy Odyssey Websites are password-protected, and search engines are asked not to index them. Photo files are stored at long, hard-to-guess addresses; anyone who is given a direct photo address could open that photo, so please share links only with people you trust.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>5. Cookies and tracking technologies</h2>
      <p>On our <strong>marketing website</strong> (legacyodyssey.com, including the blog and checkout pages) we use:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Strictly necessary (always on):</strong> to keep you signed in, to remember your language choice, to remember that a website visitor has entered the correct viewing password, and to remember your privacy choices.</li>
        <li><strong>Analytics:</strong> Google Analytics 4, Microsoft Clarity (when enabled), and Hotjar/Contentsquare, to understand how the site is used and improve it.</li>
        <li><strong>Advertising and marketing:</strong> Google Ads, Meta (Facebook) Pixel, and Pinterest Tag, to measure and improve our advertising. When you make a purchase or sign up for our emails, we may also send that event to Meta from our server (Meta Conversions API), including a hashed (scrambled) copy of your email address.</li>
        <li><strong>Affiliate tracking:</strong> Rewardful, to credit our affiliate partners when someone they referred makes a purchase.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>For visitors in the EU, UK, and EEA, non-essential (analytics and advertising) cookies load <strong>only after you consent</strong> through our cookie banner, and you can change your choice at any time using "Cookie settings." Everyone can opt out of advertising cookies and pixels at any time; see Section 10. You can also control cookies through your browser settings.</p>
      <p><strong>Legacy Odyssey Websites (your child's private website) do not load any analytics, advertising, or affiliate trackers.</strong> They use only the strictly necessary cookies described above.</p>

      <h2>6. How we share your information</h2>
      <p>We do <strong>not</strong> sell your personal information for money, and we never sell, rent, or share the content of your website (photos, videos, stories, or your child's information) for advertising. We share personal information only with service providers who process it on our behalf (our "processors" or "sub-processors"), under contracts or data processing terms, and where required by law. Our advertising partners (Google, Meta, Pinterest) receive information about visits to and purchases on our marketing website; under some US state laws (such as California's) this can count as "sharing" for advertising, and you can opt out (Section 10).</p>
