      <p>We may also disclose information if required by law or court order, or to protect the rights, property, or safety of our users or others.</p>

      <h2>7. International data transfers</h2>
      <p>We are based in the United States, and our providers may store and process data in the U.S. and other countries. If you are in the EU, UK, or another region with data-transfer restrictions, your data may be transferred outside your home country. Where required, such transfers rely on appropriate safeguards such as the European Commission's Standard Contractual Clauses (SCCs) or equivalent mechanisms offered by our providers.</p>

      <h2>8. Data retention</h2>
      <p>We keep your account and website content for as long as your plan is active. When your plan ends, whether you cancel or it is not renewed, you keep access through the end of the period you have paid for. After that, your website goes offline and we stop renewing the associated domain. We then keep your photos, videos, and content for <strong>one year</strong> so you can reactivate and pick up exactly where you left off. If you do not reactivate within that year, that website's content and account data are permanently deleted, including photos in storage and our photo backups, videos at our video provider, and your contact list. You can ask us to delete your data immediately at any time instead of waiting out the one-year window (see Section 9): just cancel and email us. We keep limited records (such as billing and transaction records, and a record of privacy requests) for as long as required to meet legal, tax, and accounting obligations. If you would rather keep your domain, you can transfer it to another registrar before its term ends.</p>
      <p>Machine translations of website text are cached so they load quickly; these display-only copies are deleted along with the website content they came from. Server error reports are kept by Sentry for a limited period under its retention settings.</p>

      <h2>9. Your privacy rights</h2>
      <p>Depending on where you live, you may have some or all of the following rights:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Access:</strong> a copy of the personal data we hold about you. You can download your data at any time from your account dashboard ("Download My Data").</li>
        <li><strong>Rectification:</strong> correct inaccurate or incomplete data (much of this you can do yourself in the app or web editor).</li>
        <li><strong>Erasure:</strong> delete your account and associated data.</li>
        <li><strong>Portability:</strong> receive your data in a portable format.</li>
        <li><strong>Restriction / Objection:</strong> limit or object to certain processing.</li>
        <li><strong>Opt out of targeted advertising, "sale," or "sharing":</strong> see Section 10.</li>
        <li><strong>Withdraw consent:</strong> for anything based on consent (for example analytics or advertising cookies), at any time, without affecting earlier processing.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>To exercise any of these, email <a href="mailto:help@legacyodyssey.com">help@legacyodyssey.com</a>. We may need to verify your identity (usually by confirming the request from the email address on your account). You can use an authorized agent; we may ask the agent for proof of your permission. We will respond within the time required by applicable law (generally within 30 days, or 45 days where US state law allows). If we decline a request, you can appeal by replying to our decision. You will not be discriminated against for exercising your rights.</p>
      <p><strong>EU/UK users:</strong> you also have the right to lodge a complaint with your local data protection authority.</p>

      <h2 id="california">10. California and other US state privacy rights, including "Do Not Sell or Share"</h2>
      <p>This section applies to residents of California (CCPA as amended by the CPRA) and of other US states with similar laws (for example Colorado, Connecticut, Virginia, Texas, and Oregon).</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Categories we collect:</strong> identifiers (name, email, IP address); customer records (billing records, domain registrant details); commercial information (purchases and gifts); internet activity on our marketing website; photos, videos, and other content you upload; and limited inferences used for advertising measurement. Sources, purposes, and recipients are described in Sections 2, 3, and 6, and retention in Section 8.</li>
        <li><strong>No sale for money.</strong> We do not sell personal information for money.</li>
        <li><strong>"Sharing" for advertising.</strong> Our marketing website uses advertising pixels from Google, Meta, and Pinterest (Section 5). Under California law, allowing these partners to collect information for cross-context behavioral advertising can be considered "sharing," and under other state laws it can be "targeted advertising." In the past 12 months, the categories involved were identifiers (such as IP address, device and cookie IDs, and a hashed email address when you purchase or sign up) and internet activity on our marketing website. <strong>Your website's content and your child's information are never shared for advertising.</strong></li>
        <li><strong>Children and teens.</strong> We do not knowingly sell or share the personal information of anyone under 16.</li>
        <li><strong>Sensitive personal information.</strong> We use it only to provide the Service you request, not to infer characteristics about you.</li>
      </ul>
      <p><strong>How to opt out.</strong> Use our <a href="/do-not-sell-or-share">Do Not Sell or Share My Personal Information</a> page. Opting out there turns off advertising pixels on our marketing website in that browser, and if you give us your email address, we also stop sending your purchase and sign-up events to advertising partners from our servers. We also honor the <strong>Global Privacy Control (GPC)</strong> signal: if your browser sends GPC, we treat it as an opt-out for that browser automatically. Analytics that help us run and improve our own website may continue.</p>
      <p>You also have the rights to know, access, correct, and delete your personal information, and not to be discriminated against for using these rights (Section 9). To make a request, email <a href="mailto:help@legacyodyssey.com">help@legacyodyssey.com</a>.</p>

      <h2>11. Your website visitors</h2>
      <p>When someone visits a Legacy Odyssey Website, we and our hosting providers (including Approximated for custom domains and Cloudflare) process minimal technical information, such as IP address and browser type, to deliver the page securely. If a visitor chooses Spanish or Hindi, we remember that choice in a cookie and send the website's text to DeepL for translation. We do not use analytics, advertising, or affiliate trackers on Legacy Odyssey Websites, and we do not track your visitors across other websites. People you add to Your Contacts can unsubscribe from update emails at any time using the link in those emails.</p>

      <h2>12. Children's privacy</h2>
      <p>The Service is intended for parents and legal guardians, who must be adults. Accounts may only be created and managed by an adult, and we do not knowingly allow children to create accounts or knowingly collect personal information directly from a child. A Legacy Odyssey Website may contain information, photos, and videos about a child, which the account holder provides and is responsible for, having the authority to do so.</p>
      <p>We design with children's privacy in mind, consistent with the U.S. Children's Online Privacy Protection Act (COPPA) and, where applicable, GDPR protections for children's data. If you believe a child has provided us personal information without proper authorization, contact us and we will delete it.</p>

      <h2>13. Data breaches</h2>
      <p>If a security incident affects your personal information, we will investigate promptly and notify you and the relevant authorities as required by applicable law.</p>

      <h2>14. Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. We will post the updated version here with a new "Last updated" date and, for material changes, notify account holders by email.</p>

      <h2>15. Contact us</h2>
      <p>Questions or concerns about this policy or how we handle your data:</p>
      <p>
        <strong>DOR Industries</strong> (Legacy Odyssey)<br>
        Mesa, Arizona, USA<br>
        Email: <a href="mailto:help@legacyodyssey.com">help@legacyodyssey.com</a>
      </p>
